# What never reaches the build context.
#
# The first block is not about image size. A file copied into an image stays in that image's
# layers whoever deletes it later, and these hold private keys - the same keys .gitignore
# keeps out of a public repo. An image is published too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.accounts.json
*.accounts.json
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
subgraph/.certs/

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`. A host copy would be whatever this laptop last
# compiled, which is not necessarily this commit.
artifacts/
cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not the coordinator's business. The subgraph is three other Fly apps built from stock
# images, and `subgraph/fly/` deploys them.
subgraph/
test/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
